Ta có: $2 \cos^2(3x) - 1 = \cos \left(x + \dfrac{\pi}{5} \right)$
$\Leftrightarrow \cos(6x) = \cos \left(x + \dfrac{\pi}{5} \right)$
$\Leftrightarrow \left[
\begin{array}{l}
6x = x + \dfrac{\pi}{5} + k2\pi\\
6x = -x - \dfrac{\pi}{5} + k2\pi
\end{array}
\right.$
$\Leftrightarrow \left[
\begin{array}{l}
5x = \dfrac{\pi}{5} + k2\pi\\
7x = -\dfrac{\pi}{5} + k2\pi
\end{array}
\right.$
$\Leftrightarrow \left[
\begin{array}{l}
x = \dfrac{\pi}{25} + \dfrac{k2\pi}{5}\\
x = -\dfrac{\pi}{35} + \dfrac{k2\pi}{7}
\end{array}
\right. \quad (k \in \mathbb{Z})$
